559	/**
560	 * Per-domain SPF / DKIM / DMARC / MX self-check.
561	 *
562	 * WHY: "my mail goes to spam" was undiagnosable from inside the product. The
563	 * platform owner hit exactly this and had to diagnose it with an external
564	 * third-party tool, so every customer in the same position had no route at all.
565	 *
566	 * Two things this panel must never do, because both would make it the codebase's
567	 * recurring defect in a new place — a surface reporting an outcome it never
568	 * verified, here telling someone their mail is fine while it goes to spam:
569	 *
570	 *   1. Report a status the server did not derive from DNS. Every badge below
571	 *      comes from `checkEmailDeliverability`, which reads the zone's own
572	 *      AUTHORITATIVE nameservers (this host's `hosts: files myhostname dns`
573	 *      nsswitch order can answer a lookup out of /etc/hosts while looking like a
574	 *      real query — that produced one confidently wrong diagnosis already).
575	 *   2. Round a partial answer up. `unknown` renders as its own slate state, not
576	 *      as a pass, and the nameservers actually queried are printed so the result
577	 *      is auditable rather than taken on trust.
578	 *
579	 * Not auto-run: each check is several outbound DNS queries plus one Mailcow call,
580	 * and the customer has to be looking at it for the answer to be useful.
581	 */
582	function DeliverabilityPanel({
583	  subscriptionId,
